{
  "as_of": "2026-09-27",
  "scope": "Request Content-Digest admission before signature inspection, DNS and dispatch in Go/Python MCP; actual-body snapshot verification in direct Go transport. Local simulated peers and loopback tests, no deployment.",
  "standards": [
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9530.html#section-2",
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8941.html"
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Share the existing response digest grammar through the Go HTTP guard; Python reuses its existing parser. No second digest grammar.",
    "Validate all declared supported SHA-256/SHA-512 values over exact outgoing content before signature inspection. Dispatch and diagnostics agree.",
    "Direct Go transport reads the actual Body at most 1 MiB plus one overflow byte, verifies it before DNS, and sends the verified snapshot. Caller GetBody is not trusted.",
    "Reject invalid declared lengths, actual-length mismatches, read errors, malformed/empty/duplicate fields and digest mismatches; close original bodies once, including cancellation.",
    "Correct digests retain all existing signature and origin controls. No new Snort SID."
  ],
