  "limits": [
    "Digest admission is a local stricter policy: RFC 9530 allows recipients to ignore digests. Optional unsigned digests neither authenticate a sender nor prove safe content; a malicious sender can omit or recompute them.",
    "Repr-Digest, Want-* fields, legacy Digest and HTTP message signatures are not implemented by this change.",
    "Direct Go cancellation requires the documented net/http.Request.Body contract that Close unblocks a concurrent Read. Arbitrary caller readers violating that contract cannot be forcibly terminated.",
    "Digest-free direct Go requests retain existing transport behavior. The direct transport does not itself run the MCP signature engine.",
    "All evidence is local. No deployed routing boundary, external endpoint, universal standards conformance or unknown-attack prevention was verified."
  ],
